; The differential probe: one source set, built natively here as the golden and
; mirrored into js/jsoo and js/melange. See .ai/js_backends_design.md.
;
; Two libraries rather than one, and two entry points rather than a flag,
; because melange can only reach the pure half: walk_core needs jsont alone and
; core needs fmt alone, while lib/native brings Bigarray (no melange support)
; and Jsont_bytesrw. Recording that boundary here as [probes_pure] vs
; [probes_native] lets js/melange copy a clean subset instead of excluding files
; by hand -- and keeps a section from silently drifting to the wrong side.
;
; [wrapped false] matches the repo convention, so the mirrors refer to
; [Probe_walk_core] etc. unqualified exactly as this directory does.

(library
 (name probes_pure)
 (wrapped false)
 (modules probe_walk_core probe_core)
 (libraries walk_core core fmt jsont))

(library
 (name probes_native)
 (wrapped false)
 (modules probe_tensor_json probe_native)
 (libraries probes_pure native native_op_walk walk_core core))

; A THIRD library, for the same reason there is a second one: it records a real
; boundary rather than grouping by convenience. Everything here reaches PyTorch
; -- pytorch_types is generated from the schema.yaml inside the modules/pytorch
; submodule -- so this tier needs a submodule checkout that the two above do not,
; and melange cannot reach any of it. Keeping it separate is what stops a
; section drifting across that line unnoticed.

(library
 (name probes_pt2)
 (wrapped false)
 (modules probe_model_json probe_pt2 probe_worker)
 (libraries
  probes_pure
  core
  fmt
  pt2
  pytorch_types
  schema_runtime
  jsont
  jsont.bytesrw
  model_explorer
  model_explorer_export
  native
  native_graph
  native_interp))

; Separate stanzas with disjoint [modules]: two singular executables cannot both
; own a module, and putting both names in one plural stanza would build each
; entry against the other's module for no reason.

; [byte] alongside [exe] is a triage tool, not an artifact anyone ships. When
; the jsoo diff goes red, running native_probe.bc under ocamlrun says
; immediately which side is at fault: js_of_ocaml compiles the BYTECODE, so a
; difference that survives between .bc and .exe is ocamlopt's, not jsoo's.
; That is how the FMA contraction described in probe_native.ml was pinned down.

(executable
 (name native_probe)
 (modes exe byte)
 (modules native_probe)
 (libraries probes_pure probes_native probes_pt2))

; The golden for jsoo.pt2.runtest. Without a native build of this source there
; is nothing for the .bc.js to be diffed against. [byte] for the same triage
; reason as native_probe above -- and a new tier is exactly where a divergence
; whose side is unclear is most likely to turn up.

(executable
 (name pt2_probe)
 (modes exe byte)
 (modules pt2_probe)
 (libraries probes_pt2))

(executable
 (name subset_probe)
 (modules subset_probe)
 (libraries probes_pure))

; The tier-1 fixture: resnet18's committed model.json, the smallest of the 17
; (224K). Same shell-copy idiom as data/dune and test/dune -- the submodule is
; excluded from dune's scan, and %{project_root} reaches it only inside
; (action ...), never (deps ...), so this carries no dep tracking. Touch this
; file or `dune clean` if the submodule moves. See .ai/dune_cram_patterns.md.

(rule
 (target model.json)
 (action
  (with-stdout-to
   %{target}
   (run
    cat
    %{project_root}/../../modules/pytorch.models.pt2/models/resnet18/models/model.json))))
